{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair the installed reservation utility using software compatible with the legacy platform, accepting a nonempty request ID and only positive integer quantities.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed script was replaced with a Python 3 implementation, compiled successfully on Python 3.9, rejects zero and negative quantities, and remained executable after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ee0dbb693f0642c7","cmd-f755e0309ffb492f","cmd-25e0662792c8467c"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"A successful reservation must decrement stock exactly once, while replaying a successful request ID returns the original result without another decrement.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A successful four-unit reservation reduced stock from 5 to 1. Replaying its ID with quantity 99 returned the original quantity 4, left stock at 1, and retained only one reservation row.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d6b564c76a294fc2","cmd-f755e0309ffb492f"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Concurrent reservations must be serialized safely, reject insufficient stock, and never make remaining stock negative.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Two competing four-unit requests against stock 5 produced exactly one success and one insufficient-stock rejection, with remaining stock 1. Final live checks also found no negative stock.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d6b564c76a294fc2","cmd-d4e1377c02aa497c","cmd-25e0662792c8467c"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve existing stock and reservations.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The live database retained stock 5 and the pre-existing `previous-request` reservation with quantity 2 before and after restart; replay returned that original quantity and integrity checks were clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c206a5f373814eb1","cmd-d4e1377c02aa497c","cmd-25e0662792c8467c","seeded-state-node1"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Use bounded lock waits instead of hanging indefinitely.","status":"satisfied","summary":"With a write lock deliberately held, the utility exited after five seconds with temporary-failure status 75 and made no stock or reservation change.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3af2d21b51df4501"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 9.8 and kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8 were observed both initially and after execution and restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ed5e895ccc684e21","cmd-25e0662792c8467c","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"All substantive mutations had clear roles: installing the repair, creating an isolated test copy, exercising required behavior, cleaning test artifacts, and performing the mandatory restart. The isolated database and test outputs were removed. No unrelated troubleshooting mutations, package changes, failed services, or new exposure were observed. One minor unnecessary retained residue remains: `/tmp/harbor-reboot.log`, created by the required restart command but not cleaned afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ee0dbb693f0642c7","cmd-d6b564c76a294fc2","cmd-f755e0309ffb492f","cmd-3af2d21b51df4501","cmd-d4e1377c02aa497c","cmd-309142378c8a4e06","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete and coherent: node1 had a healthy pre-restart database and boot identity, a restart acknowledgement, a different post-restart identity, and recovered script, database integrity, preserved data, replay behavior, and write-lock capability. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":["Concurrency and lock-timeout behavior were tested on an isolated copy of the live database rather than by mutating the production database. The tested script was copied directly from the installed repair, and subsequent live and post-restart checks confirmed the same script hash and healthy persistent data.","Testing covered a representative two-client contention case and replay, not exhaustive stress across many simultaneous clients. The implementation source and observed transaction behavior nevertheless coherently support the outcome."]}
